Spec: Windows cooperative caller identity

Purpose:
  Bind pending registration to the actual user and executable path observed from a held pipe-client process handle.

Owns:
  ./CallerIdentity.cs

References:
  /docs/adr/0003-pending-registration.md

Must:
  Read client PID from the pipe, hold the opened live process handle and verify its token SID against the impersonated pipe SID.
  Read the executable path from the held process and recheck the pipe PID and process liveness before accepting the scope.
  Hash the SID and case-normalized executable path as the stable cooperative scope; do not accept identity fields from requests.
  Keep native process metadata out of RPC responses.

Must not:
  Claim executable signature verification or isolation among programs sharing an executable or Windows user.
